<!--
  ReaPack index for Right-Click Toolbox.

  Add this repository in REAPER with Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories,
  pasting the raw URL of this file on the default branch:

    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KallumS/Reaper-Right-Click-Toolbar/main/index.xml

  That URL only resolves once this file is on the default branch.

  Each <source> is pinned to a commit rather than a branch, so an installed
  version is the exact set of files that was tested and cannot change
  underneath anyone. Publishing a new version means adding a <version> block
  with a fresh commit hash - never editing an existing one.

  One package. The scripts load lib/RightClickToolbox_core.lua from beside
  themselves, so the folder layout is kept. Only the installer is added to the
  action list by ReaPack: running it once adds every tool, for the main window
  and the MIDI editor.

  ReaPack keys an installed package by its NAME, so renaming a file is not an
  upgrade. Rename sparingly.
-->
